.TH FUSEMESH 1 "October 2026" "Fuse" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fusemesh \- evaluate FuseMesh source and write an OBJ mesh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fusemesh
[\fB--preview-line\fR \fIN\fR]
.br
.B fusemesh
[\fB--builtins\fR]
.br
.B fusemesh lsp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fusemesh
reads one FuseMesh program from standard input and writes a Wavefront OBJ
mesh to standard output. The current mesh primitive is a subdivided disk.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B lsp
Run the capability language server over JSON-RPC on standard input and output.
It provides diagnostics, receiver-aware completion, and hover documentation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --preview-line " N"
Compile the intermediate mesh selected by source line \fIN\fR.
.TP
.B --builtins
Print all FuseMesh function signatures and their descriptions.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print a short usage guide.
.SH LANGUAGE API
FuseMesh uses dot calls for mesh construction and configuration.
.PP
.nf
disk() -> mesh
radius(mesh, float) -> mesh
segments(mesh, float) -> mesh
rings(mesh, float) -> mesh
uv_radial(mesh) -> mesh
.fi
.PP
\fBdisk\fR creates a filled disk with centered planar UVs. \fBradius\fR sets
its radius. \fBsegments\fR controls angular subdivisions and \fBrings\fR
controls concentric subdivisions. \fBuv_radial\fR changes the UV map so U
runs from the center to the rim and V wraps around the circumference.
.PP
Use \fBfusemesh --builtins\fR for the complete descriptions.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
fusemesh < mesh.pmesh > mesh.obj
fusemesh --preview-line 4 < mesh.pmesh > preview.obj
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero on success and non-zero for invalid options, source, rendering,
or output errors.
